# GUI Python smoke (mandatory before “done”)

If you changed any file under `ncc_gui/` or any module `ui/gui/**/*.py`, you
**must** run this before saying the task is finished:

```bash
bash tests/gui/validate-gui-python.sh
```

It catches:

- `SettingsTabSpec` / dataclass field-order `TypeError` (AST, no Qt needed)
- `SyntaxError` via `compileall` on `ncc_gui/` and every `ui/gui/settings.py`
- Full `import ncc_gui.settings` when PySide6 is available
- Every `ui/gui/page.py` `create_page()` when PySide6 is available (incl. AI assistant)

**Do not** claim the GUI works after only a partial edit or after
`system-update` without this smoke (or equivalent import) succeeding.

If the smoke fails, fix it in the same turn — the previous failure mode was
“rebuild succeeds, `ncc` GUI crashes on import”.
